From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: nsscc-qca8k: honor reset post-deassert delay

The QCA8084 package must settle after its GPIO reset is deasserted
before the MDIO bus can access the package.  The QSDK qca_mdio_probe()
drives GPIO60 low for 100-110 ms and then high for another 100-110 ms.
The upstream NSSCC probe waits before deasserting the reset but returns
immediately afterwards, so a cold boot can access the package too early.

Read an optional "reset-post-delay-us" property and sleep for that
interval after releasing the reset.  Boards that need the QSDK timing
can set it to 100000.  The property is documented in the NSSCC binding.

Signed-off-by: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,qca8k-nsscc.yaml | 4 ++++
 drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c                                 | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,qca8k-nsscc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,qca8k-nsscc.yaml
@@ -48,7 +48,11 @@ properties:
   reset-gpios:
     description: GPIO connected to the chip
     maxItems: 1
 
+  reset-post-delay-us:
+    description:
+      Delay after deasserting reset-gpios before accessing the chip.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - clocks
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c
@@ -2168,6 +2168,7 @@ static int nss_cc_qca8k_clock_enable_and_reset(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct gpio_desc *gpiod;
 	struct clk *clk;
+	u32 post_delay_us;
 
 	clk = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(clk))
@@ -2179,6 +2180,10 @@ static int nss_cc_qca8k_clock_enable_and_reset(struct device *dev)
 	} else if (gpiod) {
 		msleep(100);
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(gpiod, 0);
+		if (!of_property_read_u32(dev->of_node,
+					  "reset-post-delay-us",
+					  &post_delay_us))
+			fsleep(post_delay_us);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-- 
